  "problems": "The chart is titled 'Women's Stretch Denim and Tops' and covers both denim and tops; no separate non-stretch chart was found. Source data is in inches; the page's cm toggle is computed client-side (value x 2.54, rounded to 1 decimal), so inches were recorded as the published unit. 'bust' is the published Chest row. Letter labels published as X-Small/Small/Medium/Large (abbreviated XS..L), each spanning three denim sizes. The France conversion list is malformed in the page data (11 entries, one cell '40<tab>42'), so it misaligns from size 30 up and was omitted; the Brazil list also has only 11 entries for 12 sizes and was omitted. Australia equals United Kingdom and was not repeated. The US URL geo-redirects to /en-fr/ in a browser; data read from the page's embedded size_guide script."
